  "deliverable": {
    "kind": "document",
    "description": "Security review of the lending-vault code at commit 7c1e4b9a2d3f5068a1b2c3d4e5f60718293a4b5c. Scope: contracts/Vault.sol, contracts/InterestModel.sol and contracts/PriceFeed.sol. Deliver one JSON report with the commit reviewed, the files reviewed and the findings; it may add a summary, the report's date and a salt of 32 random bytes that keeps its fingerprint from being guessed. Each finding has an id, a severity, a title, one or more locations, the root cause and a recommended fix; it may add its impact and a status (open, fixed or acknowledged). Each location names a file in scope and may add a line range and the code excerpt it is about. A finding rated Medium or higher also carries the proof-of-concept files that show it. Severity scale: Critical, anyone can take or lock funds with no special access; High, funds can be taken or locked only with a precondition such as a privileged role or an unusual market state; Medium, the code breaks a stated rule or loses a bounded amount; Low, a defect that puts no funds at risk; Info, a note on clarity, style or cost. A report with no findings is a complete report.",
    "format": "application/json"
  },
